{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from majestic-depilatory-beetle. The advisory `sweep (windows)` job deselects the 133 tests (58 modules) in `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/text-encoding.args` (runs at `b4e0d01b649`, 2026-11-15/16). On Windows (Python 3.11-3.14) text I/O without `encoding=` uses the ANSI code page (cp1252) and writes translate `\\n` to `\\r\\n`.\n\nRoot causes, confirmed from Windows job 133527199439 (run 43932173744) and a local run of the 133 tests under `PYTHONWARNDEFAULTENCODING=1 -W always::EncodingWarning` (Python reports every locale-default text call):\n\n1. **Build hook writes the generated module in cp1252 (product; most of the 133).** `hatch_build.py:112` `target.write_text(...)` has no `encoding`, so the em dash in the generated `src/rebar/_build_info.py` docstring is byte `0x97`. Every whole-tree scan that reads `src/rebar/**/*.py` as UTF-8 (`tests/_tree_scan.py:40`, `scripts/gen_env_registry.py:320`, packaging/wheel checks) then fails with `UnicodeDecodeError: 'utf-8' codec can't decode byte 0x97 in position 45`. `_read_existing_commit` (`hatch_build.py:65`) also raises on such a stale file instead of degrading.\n2. **CLI stdout is cp1252 (product).** `rebar explain plan` writes guide text containing characters cp1252 cannot encode (`src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py:290`), so the command exits 1 with `UnicodeEncodeError: 'charmap' codec can't encode` whenever stdout is a pipe.\n3. **`bindings.json` written with CRLF (product).** `src/rebar/reconciler/binding_repository.py:76` opens with `os.fdopen(fd, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\")` and no `newline`, so the canonical file becomes `{\\r\\n ...` (6 tests in `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_binding_repository.py`).\n4. **Test-side reads/writes without `encoding`.** Tests read UTF-8 docs/workflows with the locale codec (`'charmap' codec can't decode byte 0x90/0x8f/0x9d`) or write fixtures that product code then reads as UTF-8; e.g. `tests/unit/test_alarm_actions_terraform.py:142`, `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:84`, `tests/unit/test_snapshot_docs.py:16`, `tests/unit/workflow/test_cli.py:65,99`; `tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py:493` builds its expected bytes in text mode (CRLF); `tests/unit/test_caplog_coverage_integrity.py` decodes a pytester child's cp1252 stdout as UTF-8.\n\n## Approach\n\nMake UTF-8 explicit at each boundary, in the product first:\n\n- `hatch_build.py`: `write_text(..., encoding=\"utf-8\")`; `_read_existing_commit` also treats `UnicodeDecodeError` as \"no baked SHA\".\n- `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py` `main` (`:306`): when `sys.stdout`/`sys.stderr` is an `io.TextIOWrapper` whose encoding is not UTF-8, `reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\")`, so rebar's output is UTF-8 on every host (a no-op on Linux/macOS and under pytest capture).\n- `binding_repository.py:76`: add `newline=\"\\n\"`.\n- The 17 other locale-default text calls under `src/rebar` that ruff's PLW1514 reports get `encoding=\"utf-8\"`: `_commands/compact_trigger.py:140`, `_commands/fsck_repair.py:419`, `_engine_support/bridge_fsck_drift.py:21`, `_engine_support/next_batch.py:203`, `_snapshot/gc_trigger.py:131`, `llm/evals/engine_comparison.py:65,413`, `llm/evals/eval_solver.py:40,52`, `reconciler/apply_planning.py:143,175,235`, `reconciler/pass_io.py:186`, `reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py:281`, `reconciler/sync_logger.py:32`, `reducer/marker.py:24,53`. Likewise the 5 in `scripts`: `check_verify_gate_parity.py:86`, `measure_baseline_normalization.py:188`, `plan_review_contamination_rate.py:66`, `retarget_jira_project.py:39`, `run_live_matrix.py:72`. (`src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py` is rewritten by bug leafy-gorillian-gnat and `scripts/check_deploy_manifest.py` by bug arctic-unsecular-esok; each adds `encoding` there.)\n- Each failing test gets `encoding=\"utf-8\"` (and bytes comparison where it compares bytes); the pytester child in `test_caplog_coverage_integrity.py` gets `PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8` via `monkeypatch.setenv`.\n\nA lint rule is not adopted: PLW1514 is preview-only in ruff 0.16.3 and does not flag `hatch_build.py:112` (it cannot infer the `Path` receiver) or `subprocess` `text=True`, so it would not have caught root cause 1. This is recorded on the ticket. No config key, env var or flag is added.\n\nRemove each fixed line from `text-encoding.args`; delete the file and its `@` line in `.github/workflows/test.yml` once empty.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `hatch_build.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py`, `src/rebar/reconciler/binding_repository.py`, and the 17 `src/rebar` and 5 `scripts` sites listed above\n- The failing test modules listed in `text-encoding.args` that read or write text without `encoding` (e.g. `tests/unit/test_alarm_actions_terraform.py`, `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py`, `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py`, `tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py`, `tests/unit/test_caplog_coverage_integrity.py`, `tests/unit/conftest.py`, `tests/_build_provenance_fixture.py`)\n- New regression tests: `tests/unit/test_windows_text_encoding.py`\n- `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/text-encoding.args`, `.github/workflows/test.yml`\n\n## Testing\n\nNew `tests/unit/test_windows_text_encoding.py`, each failing before its fix on Linux:\n- runs the hatch hook's `initialize` in a subprocess under `-X warn_default_encoding -W error::EncodingWarning` and asserts the generated file decodes as UTF-8; edge: a cp1252 stale `_build_info.py` yields no baked SHA instead of raising.\n- runs `python -m rebar explain plan` with `PYTHONIOENCODING=cp1252` and asserts exit 0 and UTF-8 output.\n- saves a `BindingRepository` with `os.fdopen` routed through `_pyio.open` and `os.linesep` patched to `\"\\r\\n\"` (the pure-Python I/O reads `os.linesep` at write time; confirmed locally), and asserts the file contains no `\\r`.\n\nThe 133 listed tests pass under `make verify`; Windows: `gh workflow run test.yml --ref main` after merge.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The class's root cause is recorded on this ticket with the evidence that confirmed it.\n- [ ] Each new regression test fails against the pre-fix code and passes after (outcomes recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] Every line removed from `text-encoding.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `sweep (windows)` concludes `success` on that run.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795026487083822429,"uuid":"5233528a-39db-4dfc-96af-ddd3fccfc41c"}